@integrations/skills/sigil/design-compilation-review.sigil import { SigilDesignCompilationReview }
@integrations/skills/sigil/review-gate.sigil import { SigilReviewGate }

component SigilGlossaryWorkflow {
  goal {
    Keep reviewed project vocabulary coherent through separate deterministic
    inspection, model-assisted candidate extraction, and explicitly approved
    glossary mutation.
  }

  interface {
GlossaryWorkflow {
      validates deterministic glossary diagnostics before semantic review

      extracts candidate domain terms and conflicting usage from Sigil prose

      separates deterministic glossary projection inspection from mandatory
      model-assisted candidate extraction

      reports candidate evidence or an explicit evidence-based no-material-candidate
      result after accepted post-write DesignCompilationReview evidence and before
      the next applicable implementation ReviewGate

      classifies every Sigil session as glossary extraction required, extraction
      deferred, or deterministic inspection only

      reports the selected glossary status and its evidence instead of silently
      skipping candidate identification

      presents exact reviewed GlossaryFile proposals without automatically changing
      authority

      requires post-write glossary inspection and candidate extraction after approved
      Sigil is created or semantically edited

      carries relevant reviewed terminology into implementation context

      includes a glossary eval fixture covering extraction, ambiguity, context
      placement, and approval
    }
  }
}

expand SigilGlossaryWorkflow {
  logic {
GlossaryWorkflow {
      Collect candidate terms with their source occurrences and resolved bounded
      contexts.

      Separate accepted glossary authority from model-assisted candidate extraction.

      When GlossaryFile exists, perform deterministic glossary inspection and
      explicitly classify whether model-assisted extraction applies.

      Begin model-assisted glossary candidate extraction only after the post-write
      and post-grouping DesignCompilationReview is green or every yellow finding has
      been explicitly reviewed and accepted as nonblocking for the selected scope.

      When concept grouping is unnecessary, the post-write DesignCompilationReview
      directly gates glossary candidate extraction.

      After every approved Sigil write or semantic edit, run deterministic glossary
      and workspace inspection, then independently perform model-assisted extraction
      from the changed semantic units regardless of diagnostic count or GlossaryFile
      presence.

      Require model-assisted extraction after an approved semantic Sigil write or
      edit, when the user requests vocabulary review, or when terminology ambiguity
      materially affects the selected scope.

      For an explicit vocabulary review or material ambiguity without changed Sigil,
      extract from the selected loaded Sigil scope only after DesignCompilationReview
      is green or every yellow finding has been explicitly reviewed and accepted as
      nonblocking.

      When design compilation is unavailable, incomplete, red, or has an unresolved
      yellow finding, report extraction as deferred and name the blocking review
      state.

      When a session changes only implementation or performs read-only work without a
      vocabulary-review trigger, report deterministic inspection only and explain
      that no semantic Sigil lines entered candidate extraction.

      Conclude that no material candidate exists only after inspecting the changed
      semantic units, relevant surrounding occurrences, and accepted glossary
      entries.

      Before completing a triggered session, report candidates with evidence or an
      evidence-based no-material-candidate result.

      Report conflicting definitions, aliases, scope placement, and
      normative-contract drift.

      Present exact JSON additions, replacements, or removals to ReviewGate with
      glossary-change before mutation.

      After approved Sigil is written or semantically edited, run workspace and
      glossary validation and inspect changed semantic units for candidate terms.

      Block review and implementation when undefined or conflicting terminology could
      materially alter behavior, ownership, state, APIs, or implementation.

      After ReviewGate for glossary-change returns ready, write only the accepted
      proposal, rerun glossary and workspace validation, and return to ReviewGate for
      implementation.

      Before implementation, obtain context through sigil context and make its scoped
      glossary projection available to the coding agent.
    }
  }

  constraints {
GlossaryWorkflow {
      Candidate extraction never becomes authoritative without explicit human
      approval.

      Normative approved Sigil governs when GlossaryFile conflicts with a component
      contract.

      Unknown vocabulary remains a semantic-review candidate rather than a
      deterministic core diagnostic.

      Zero diagnostics from sigil glossary establishes only that the deterministic
      glossary projection is valid; it never proves the absence of unknown candidate
      vocabulary, conflicting meanings, or incorrect scope.

      A host does not report that no glossary changes are needed until model-assisted
      candidate extraction is complete and its evidence is recorded.

      Ordinary unambiguous vocabulary does not block review merely because it is
      absent from GlossaryFile.

      Material terminology ambiguity blocks implementation until its reviewed
      definition, aliases, and workspace or bounded-context scope are approved.

      Coding agents use scoped glossary context to interpret requests and Sigil
      without treating glossary definitions as behavioral contracts.

      Markdown extraction remains deferred from the initial fixture and workflow.
    }
  }

  decisions {
GlossaryWorkflow {
      Decision: Make glossary routing and completion status explicit in every Sigil
      session while keeping model-assisted extraction scope-triggered and
      semantic-readiness-gated.

      Scope: Governs sessions using the Sigil skill when a GlossaryFile exists,
      approved Sigil is written or edited, vocabulary review is requested, or
      material terminology ambiguity is identified; excludes unrelated implementation
      prose and deferred Markdown extraction.

      Trade-offs: Every Sigil session gains a small deterministic inspection and
      reporting cost, while implementation-only sessions avoid repeated full
      candidate extraction.

      Design issues addressed: Silent routing and removal of glossary language from
      the host prompt made correctly deferred or inapplicable extraction appear not
      to run.

      Discarded alternatives: Extracting candidates from the entire workspace in
      every session would create repeated noise and could bypass semantic-readiness
      ordering.

      Consequences: Triggered extraction cannot disappear silently, deferred
      extraction names its blocker, and inspection-only sessions explain why
      candidate identification did not apply.

      Revisit when: Deterministic tooling can identify candidate vocabulary or the
      host exposes workflow-stage status directly.
    }
  }

  cases {
GlossaryWorkflow {
      Two inconsistent uses of one candidate term produce a review question rather
      than an inferred definition.

      A zero-diagnostic glossary projection followed by a changed semantic unit
      containing an unknown project-specific term still produces candidate evidence
      and, when material, an exact glossary proposal.

      When model-assisted inspection finds no material candidate, the host records
      the changed lines and surrounding evidence inspected before proceeding to Sigil
      review.

      An approved Sigil edit with no material terminology candidate proceeds to
      ReviewGate for implementation after workspace and glossary validation.

      A correction-required session reports glossary extraction as deferred and names
      the unresolved semantic blocker.

      An implementation-only session with no semantic Sigil edit reports
      deterministic inspection only rather than implying candidate extraction
      completed.

      An explicit vocabulary-review request extracts candidates from the selected
      semantically aligned Sigil scope even when no Sigil line changed.

      An approved candidate is written to its selected workspace or bounded-context
      scope, validated, and returned to ReviewGate for implementation.

      A coding handoff includes only glossary terms relevant to the selected
      component or file and related sources.
    }
  }
}
